IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part III, Premiums: section 65.21 (the actuary) and
-- sections 66 to 66.6 (how the premium rate for a year is set, by whom, by when, on what information).
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5) from the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. No seat. Most of these rules are duties of officials (the Commission, the
-- Ministers, the actuary, the Governor in Council); they are encoded for what they decide: when each must act,
-- what each must provide, and what limits the rate they may set. The seat layer (ei3-seat.l4) asks the person's
-- questions over the other modules; no question there rests on this one except where it says so.
--
-- Conventions (from the keel's NOTES.md): a rate is a NUMBER fraction (1.63% is 0.0163); a date is built with YMD;
-- every rule has its own GIVEN; a judgment the law hands to an office is a BOOLEAN input named for the judgment.
-- "In a year" in ss 66(9), 66.1, 66.2, 66.3, 66.31 and 66.32 is the calendar year in which the step is taken; the
-- rate it concerns is the rate "for the following year". A step is "on or before" a day: that day counts.

§ `Section 65.21 - the actuary`

-- src:1131 | 65.21 In this Part, actuary means the Fellow of the Canadian Institute of Actuaries whose services are engaged by the Commission under subsection 28(4) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65.21 "actuary" (src:1131)
GIVEN `is a Fellow of the Canadian Institute of Actuaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has services engaged by the Commission under subsection 28(4) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65.21 actuary` IF
        `is a Fellow of the Canadian Institute of Actuaries`
    AND `has services engaged by the Commission under subsection 28(4) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`

§ `Section 66 - annual premium rate setting`

-- The seven-year period "that commences at the beginning of that year": the year's first day to the last day of the
-- sixth following year.
-- src:1136 | 66 (1) Subject to subsection (7) and section 66.32, the Commission shall set the premium rate for each year in order to generate just enough premium revenue to ensure that, at the end of the seven-year period that commences at the beginning of that year, the total of the amounts credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account after December 31, 2008 is equal to the total of the amounts charged to that Account after that date.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(1) (src:1136)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 66(1) the seven-year period that commences at the beginning of the year` IS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD year 1 1), (YMD (year PLUS 6) 12 31)

-- The object the Commission sets the rate to reach. The two totals are forecasts for the end of the seven-year
-- period; the section does not say who forecasts them (the actuary's report, s 66.3, is the evident source).
-- "Just enough" is read as equality of the two totals; the text gives no tolerance (fork F-ei3-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1136 | 66 (1) Subject to subsection (7) and section 66.32, the Commission shall set the premium rate for each year in order to generate just enough premium revenue to ensure that, at the end of the seven-year period that commences at the beginning of that year, the total of the amounts credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account after December 31, 2008 is equal to the total of the amounts charged to that Account after that date.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(1) (src:1136)
GIVEN `the total of the amounts credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account after December 31, 2008` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the amounts charged to that Account after that date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66(1) the premium rate generates just enough premium revenue` IF
    `the total of the amounts credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account after December 31, 2008`
        EQUALS `the total of the amounts charged to that Account after that date`

-- Paragraph (c) is repealed; (d) and (e) are conditional on there being such regulations or such a change.
-- src:1139 | (2) The Commission shall set the premium rate based on
-- src:1140 | (a) the information provided under sections 66.1 and 66.2;
-- src:1141 | (b) the actuary’s report provided under section 66.3 for that year;
-- src:1142 | (c) [Repealed, 2012, c. 19, s. 609]
-- src:1143 | (d) any regulations made under section 69;
-- src:1144 | (e) any changes, announced by the Minister on or before July 22 in a year, to payments to be made under paragraph 77(1)(a), (b) or (c) during the following year; and
-- src:1145 | (f) any other information that the Commission considers relevant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(2) (src:1139-1145)
GIVEN `the rate is based on the information provided under sections 66.1 and 66.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate is based on the actuary's report provided under section 66.3 for that year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations have been made under section 69` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate is based on any regulations made under section 69` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister announced, on or before July 22, a change to payments to be made under paragraph 77(1)(a), (b) or (c) during the following year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate is based on any such change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers other information relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate is based on that other information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66(2) the Commission has set the premium rate on the factors the Act names` IF
        `the rate is based on the information provided under sections 66.1 and 66.2`
    AND `the rate is based on the actuary's report provided under section 66.3 for that year`
    AND ((NOT `regulations have been made under section 69`) OR `the rate is based on any regulations made under section 69`)
    AND ((NOT `the Minister announced, on or before July 22, a change to payments to be made under paragraph 77(1)(a), (b) or (c) during the following year`) OR `the rate is based on any such change`)
    AND ((NOT `the Commission considers other information relevant`) OR `the rate is based on that other information`)

-- src:1149 | (7) The premium rate may not be increased or decreased by more than five one-hundredths of one per cent (0.05%) from one year to the next.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(7) (src:1149)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(7) the maximum change in the premium rate from one year to the next` MEANS 0.05%

-- Subsection (8) lets the Governor in Council change that maximum: when it has, the figure in force is the new one.
-- src:1152 | (8) On the joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance, the Governor in Council may change the maximum percentage referred to in subsection (7) by which the premium rate may be increased or decreased from one year to the next, if the Governor in Council considers it to be in the public interest.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(8) (src:1152)
GIVEN `the maximum percentage fixed by the Governor in Council, if it has changed the maximum` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 66(8) the maximum change in force` IS
    CONSIDER `the maximum percentage fixed by the Governor in Council, if it has changed the maximum`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 66(7) the maximum change in the premium rate from one year to the next`
    WHEN JUST changed THEN changed

-- src:1152 | (8) On the joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance, the Governor in Council may change the maximum percentage referred to in subsection (7) by which the premium rate may be increased or decreased from one year to the next, if the Governor in Council considers it to be in the public interest.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(8) (src:1152)
GIVEN `there is a joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Governor in Council considers it to be in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66(8) the Governor in Council may change the maximum percentage` IF
        `there is a joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance`
    AND `the Governor in Council considers it to be in the public interest`

-- src:1187 | (2) Subsection 66(7) does not apply to the setting of the premium rate under subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.32(2) (src:1187)
GIVEN `the rate is set by the Governor in Council under subsection 66.32(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.32(2) subsection 66(7) applies to the setting of the premium rate` IF
    NOT `the rate is set by the Governor in Council under subsection 66.32(1)`

-- "More than" the maximum is the bar, so a change of exactly the maximum is allowed, up or down.
-- src:1149 | (7) The premium rate may not be increased or decreased by more than five one-hundredths of one per cent (0.05%) from one year to the next.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(7) (src:1149)
GIVEN `the premium rate for the previous year` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium rate for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum change in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` IF
    (IF `the premium rate for the year` AT LEAST `the premium rate for the previous year`
     THEN `the premium rate for the year` MINUS `the premium rate for the previous year`
     ELSE `the premium rate for the previous year` MINUS `the premium rate for the year`)
        AT MOST `the maximum change in force`

-- Section 66.32(2) lifts the limit for a rate set by the Governor in Council under 66.32(1).
-- src:1149 | (7) The premium rate may not be increased or decreased by more than five one-hundredths of one per cent (0.05%) from one year to the next.
-- src:1187 | (2) Subsection 66(7) does not apply to the setting of the premium rate under subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(7), s 66.32(2) (src:1149) (src:1187)
GIVEN `the premium rate for the previous year` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium rate for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum change in force` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate is set by the Governor in Council under subsection 66.32(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66(7) the premium rate may be set as it is` IF
        (NOT `s 66.32(2) subsection 66(7) applies to the setting of the premium rate` `the rate is set by the Governor in Council under subsection 66.32(1)`)
    OR  `s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` `the premium rate for the previous year` `the premium rate for the year` `the maximum change in force`

-- src:1154 | (9) On or before September 14 in a year, the Commission shall set the premium rate for the following year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(9) (src:1154)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 66(9) the day on or before which the Commission shall set the premium rate for the following year` IS
    YMD year 9 14

-- src:1154 | (9) On or before September 14 in a year, the Commission shall set the premium rate for the following year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66(9) (src:1154)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the Commission set the premium rate for the following year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66(9) the Commission set the premium rate in time` IF
    `the day on which the Commission set the premium rate for the following year`
        AT MOST `s 66(9) the day on or before which the Commission shall set the premium rate for the following year` year

§ `Sections 66.1 to 66.3 - information and the actuary's report`

-- src:1156 | 66.1 (1) The Minister shall, on or before July 22 in a year, provide the actuary and the Commission with the following information:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.1(1) (src:1156)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 66.1(1) the day on or before which the Minister shall provide the information` IS
    YMD year 7 22

-- Paragraph (a) only bites if the Minister has made an announcement referred to in paragraph 66(2)(e);
-- paragraph (d) is "any prescribed information", whose prescription (66.1(2)) is machinery and not in this text.
-- src:1156 | 66.1 (1) The Minister shall, on or before July 22 in a year, provide the actuary and the Commission with the following information:
-- src:1157 | (a) if the Minister has made an announcement referred to in paragraph 66(2)(e), the forecast change in the amount of the payments to be made during each of the following seven years under paragraph 77(1)(a), (b) or (c), as the case may be;
-- src:1158 | (b) the forecast costs to be paid under paragraphs 77(1)(d), (d.1) and (g) during each of the following seven years, including any forecast change in those costs resulting from any change to the payments referred to in paragraph (a);
-- src:1159 | (c) the total of the amounts charged to the Employment Insurance Operating Account as of the last day of the most recent month for which that total is known by the Minister; and
-- src:1160 | (d) any prescribed information.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.1(1) (src:1156-1160)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the Minister provided the information` IS A DATE
      `the Minister provided it to the actuary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister provided it to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has made an announcement referred to in paragraph 66(2)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the forecast change in payments under paragraph 77(1)(a), (b) or (c) for each of the following seven years was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the forecast costs under paragraphs 77(1)(d), (d.1) and (g) for each of the following seven years were provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total charged to the Account as of the last day of the most recent month known to the Minister was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all prescribed information was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` IF
        `the day on which the Minister provided the information` AT MOST `s 66.1(1) the day on or before which the Minister shall provide the information` year
    AND `the Minister provided it to the actuary`
    AND `the Minister provided it to the Commission`
    AND ((NOT `the Minister has made an announcement referred to in paragraph 66(2)(e)`) OR `the forecast change in payments under paragraph 77(1)(a), (b) or (c) for each of the following seven years was provided`)
    AND `the forecast costs under paragraphs 77(1)(d), (d.1) and (g) for each of the following seven years were provided`
    AND `the total charged to the Account as of the last day of the most recent month known to the Minister was provided`
    AND `all prescribed information was provided`

-- src:1164 | 66.2 (1) The Minister of Finance shall, on or before July 22 in a year, provide the actuary and the Commission with the following information:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.2(1) (src:1164)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 66.2(1) the day on or before which the Minister of Finance shall provide the information` IS
    YMD year 7 22

-- src:1164 | 66.2 (1) The Minister of Finance shall, on or before July 22 in a year, provide the actuary and the Commission with the following information:
-- src:1165 | (a) the most current available forecast values of the economic variables that are relevant to the determination under section 66 of a premium rate for the following year;
-- src:1166 | (b) the amounts forecast under subparagraphs 77.1(a)(i) and (ii) and the total estimated under subparagraph 77.1(a)(iii); and
-- src:1167 | (c) any prescribed information.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.2(1) (src:1164-1167)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the Minister of Finance provided the information` IS A DATE
      `the Minister of Finance provided it to the actuary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Finance provided it to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the most current available forecast values of the relevant economic variables were provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts forecast under subparagraphs 77.1(a)(i) and (ii) and the total estimated under subparagraph 77.1(a)(iii) were provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all prescribed information was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.2(1) the Minister of Finance has provided the information` IF
        `the day on which the Minister of Finance provided the information` AT MOST `s 66.2(1) the day on or before which the Minister of Finance shall provide the information` year
    AND `the Minister of Finance provided it to the actuary`
    AND `the Minister of Finance provided it to the Commission`
    AND `the most current available forecast values of the relevant economic variables were provided`
    AND `the amounts forecast under subparagraphs 77.1(a)(i) and (ii) and the total estimated under subparagraph 77.1(a)(iii) were provided`
    AND `all prescribed information was provided`

-- src:1171 | 66.3 The actuary shall prepare actuarial forecasts and estimates for the purposes of sections 4, 66 and 69 and shall, on or before August 22 in a year, provide the Commission with a report that sets out
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.3 (src:1171)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 66.3 the day on or before which the actuary shall provide the report` IS
    YMD year 8 22

-- src:1171 | 66.3 The actuary shall prepare actuarial forecasts and estimates for the purposes of sections 4, 66 and 69 and shall, on or before August 22 in a year, provide the Commission with a report that sets out
-- src:1172 | (a) the forecast premium rate for the following year and a detailed analysis in support of the forecast;
-- src:1173 | (b) the calculations performed for the purposes of sections 4 and 69;
-- src:1174 | (c) the information provided under section 66.1; and
-- src:1175 | (d) the source of the data, the actuarial and economic assumptions and the actuarial methodology used.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.3 (src:1171-1175)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the actuary provided the report to the Commission` IS A DATE
      `the report sets out the forecast premium rate for the following year and a detailed analysis in support` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report sets out the calculations performed for the purposes of sections 4 and 69` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report sets out the information provided under section 66.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report sets out the source of the data, the actuarial and economic assumptions and the actuarial methodology used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.3 the actuary has provided the report` IF
        `the day on which the actuary provided the report to the Commission` AT MOST `s 66.3 the day on or before which the actuary shall provide the report` year
    AND `the report sets out the forecast premium rate for the following year and a detailed analysis in support`
    AND `the report sets out the calculations performed for the purposes of sections 4 and 69`
    AND `the report sets out the information provided under section 66.1`
    AND `the report sets out the source of the data, the actuarial and economic assumptions and the actuarial methodology used`

§ `Section 66.31 - report, summary, public and Parliament`

-- src:1177 | 66.31 (1) The Commission shall, on or before August 31 in a year, provide the Minister and the Minister of Finance with the report referred to in section 66.3 and a summary of that report.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.31(1) (src:1177)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 66.31(1) the day on or before which the Commission shall provide the report and summary` IS
    YMD year 8 31

-- src:1177 | 66.31 (1) The Commission shall, on or before August 31 in a year, provide the Minister and the Minister of Finance with the report referred to in section 66.3 and a summary of that report.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.31(1) (src:1177)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the Commission provided the report and a summary` IS A DATE
      `the Commission provided them to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission provided them to the Minister of Finance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.31(1) the Commission has provided the report and summary` IF
        `the day on which the Commission provided the report and a summary` AT MOST `s 66.31(1) the day on or before which the Commission shall provide the report and summary` year
    AND `the Commission provided them to the Minister`
    AND `the Commission provided them to the Minister of Finance`

-- Made available "on the day on which a premium rate is set under section 66 or 66.32".
-- src:1179 | (2) The Commission shall, on the day on which a premium rate is set under section 66 or 66.32, make available to the public the report and its summary.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.31(2) (src:1179)
GIVEN `the day on which the premium rate was set` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission made the report and its summary available to the public` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.31(2) the Commission has made the report and summary available to the public in time` IF
    `the day on which the Commission made the report and its summary available to the public`
        EQUALS `the day on which the premium rate was set`

-- "On any of the next 10 days during which that House is sitting": the sitting day is counted from 1, the first
-- sitting day of the House after the day the rate was set. One rule for one House; the next rule asks it of both.
-- src:1181 | (3) After a premium rate is set, the Minister shall cause the report and its summary to be laid before each House of Parliament on any of the next 10 days during which that House is sitting.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.31(3) (src:1181)
GIVEN `the number of the sitting day on which the report and summary were laid, counting the first sitting day after the premium rate was set as 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before a House in time` IF
        `the number of the sitting day on which the report and summary were laid, counting the first sitting day after the premium rate was set as 1` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the number of the sitting day on which the report and summary were laid, counting the first sitting day after the premium rate was set as 1` AT MOST 10

-- src:1181 | (3) After a premium rate is set, the Minister shall cause the report and its summary to be laid before each House of Parliament on any of the next 10 days during which that House is sitting.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.31(3) (src:1181)
GIVEN `the sitting day on which it was laid before the House of Commons` IS A NUMBER
      `the sitting day on which it was laid before the Senate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before each House of Parliament in time` IF
        `s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before a House in time` `the sitting day on which it was laid before the House of Commons`
    AND `s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before a House in time` `the sitting day on which it was laid before the Senate`

§ `Section 66.32 - premium rate setting by the Governor in Council`

-- src:1183 | 66.32 (1) On the joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance, the Governor in Council may, on or before September 30 in a year,
-- src:1184 | (a) if the Governor in Council considers it to be in the public interest, substitute a premium rate for the following year that is different from the one set by the Commission under section 66; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.32(1)(a) (src:1183-1184)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `there is a joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Governor in Council considers it to be in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Governor in Council acts` IS A DATE
      `the premium rate substituted for the following year` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium rate the Commission set under section 66` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.32(1)(a) the Governor in Council may substitute a premium rate` IF
        `there is a joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance`
    AND `the day on which the Governor in Council acts` AT MOST (YMD year 9 30)
    AND `the Governor in Council considers it to be in the public interest`
    AND NOT (`the premium rate substituted for the following year` EQUALS `the premium rate the Commission set under section 66`)

-- The Commission has "not set" a rate by September 14 if it set none, or set it later (a rate set on the 14th is in time, s 66(9)).
-- src:1183 | 66.32 (1) On the joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance, the Governor in Council may, on or before September 30 in a year,
-- src:1185 | (b) if the Commission has not set a premium rate under that section by September 14 in the year, set one for the following year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.32(1)(b) (src:1183) (src:1185)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `there is a joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Governor in Council acts` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission set a premium rate under section 66, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.32(1)(b) the Governor in Council may set the premium rate` IF
        `there is a joint recommendation of the Minister and the Minister of Finance`
    AND `the day on which the Governor in Council acts` AT MOST (YMD year 9 30)
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the Commission set a premium rate under section 66, if it did`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST setOn THEN setOn GREATER THAN `s 66(9) the day on or before which the Commission shall set the premium rate for the following year` year)

§ `Sections 66.4 to 66.6 - rounding, publication, the Service Fees Act`

-- Rounded to the nearest 0.01% (one hundredth of one per cent), the higher when exactly between two.
-- A rate that has no fraction of one per cent is already a multiple of 0.01%, so rounding leaves it alone.
-- src:1189 | 66.4 If the calculation of a premium rate under section 66 or 66.32 results in a rate that includes a fraction of one per cent, the resulting percentage is to be rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent or, if the resulting percentage is equidistant from two one-hundredths of one percent, to the higher of them.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.4 (src:1189)
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 66.4 the premium rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent` IS
    (FLOOR ((rate DIVIDED BY (0.01%)) PLUS 0.5)) TIMES (0.01%)

-- src:1191 | 66.5 As soon as possible after a premium rate is set under section 66 or 66.32, the Commission shall publish it in Part I of the Canada Gazette.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.5 (src:1191)
GIVEN `the Commission published the rate in Part I of the Canada Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so as soon as possible after the premium rate was set under section 66 or 66.32` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.5 the Commission has published the premium rate as required` IF
        `the Commission published the rate in Part I of the Canada Gazette`
    AND `it did so as soon as possible after the premium rate was set under section 66 or 66.32`

-- The Act says the Service Fees Act does NOT apply to these things; it says nothing about anything else, so for
-- anything else the answer is NOTHING (not covered), never TRUE or FALSE.
-- src:1193 | 66.6 For greater certainty, the Service Fees Act does not apply in respect of the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32 or the premiums determined under sections 67 and 68.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 66.6 (src:1193)
GIVEN `the matter is the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32, or the premiums determined under sections 67 and 68` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66.6 the Service Fees Act applies` IS
    IF `the matter is the premium rate set under section 66 or 66.32, or the premiums determined under sections 67 and 68`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
